# SwiftFormat — ZynSign.
#
# Two execution modes share this one rule set:
#   check  — pull requests (Scripts/ci/format.sh check, swiftformat --lint)
#   apply  — weekly maintenance (Scripts/ci/format.sh apply)
#
# Because both modes use the identical, explicitly listed rules, a green
# check guarantees the maintenance run has nothing to change: formatting
# never creates noisy commits. The rules are the cosmetic ones the
# codebase already satisfies; style decisions SwiftFormat could rewrite
# (self-insertion, wrapping, trailing commas, semicolon splitting) are
# deliberately left off — compact semicolon-joined statements are an
# established house style in this repository.

--rules trailingSpace,consecutiveBlankLines

# Consistency anchors if a listed rule ever needs context.
--indent 4

--exclude build,DerivedData,.build,.external-validation,node_modules,Reports
